Title: FEDERAL TRACE
Episode: 101 "Chain of Custody"
Credit: Original fixture material written for the Canon AI test harness.

COLD OPEN

EXT. RIVERGATE RAIL YARD - PRE-DAWN

A FEDERAL EVIDENCE VAN crawls between freight cars. Rain clicks against the sealed cargo box.

Inside the van, TECHNICIAN LEO MART keeps one hand on a metal case stamped FT-401 / FEDERAL PROPERTY.

A black SUV blocks the service road. Two masked figures move with practiced speed.

MART
Chain log says I hand this to a person, not a ghost.

The taller figure shows a laminated badge with the photo scratched white.

MASKED FIGURE
Then write down ghost.

The cargo seal snaps. The metal case disappears into the rain.

END COLD OPEN.

ACT ONE

INT. FBI RIVERGATE FIELD OFFICE - BULLPEN - MORNING

The bullpen is all glass walls, case boards, and bad coffee. Screens read CASE FT-401 / EVIDENCE TRANSPORT HIT.

SSA RUTH KEENE, 50s, runs the room without raising her voice. SPECIAL AGENT LENA ORTIZ, 30s, pins rail-yard photos beside a map. SPECIAL AGENT MALIK SHAW, 40s, drops a wet field jacket on a chair.

PRIYA SEN, 20s, cyber analyst, wheels over a laptop cart. DR. DARIUS CHO, 40s, forensic analyst, bags a smear of black gel from Mart's sleeve.

KEENE
This is a Bureau case until I say otherwise. No locals on the chain log, no calls outside the room.

MALIK
The hijack crew knew the van route, the seal number, and Mart's coffee order.

PRIYA
Give me the tower dump and I'll rebuild the van's route before lunch.

Lena holds up a green transit card in an evidence sleeve.

LENA
The hijacker dropped a Meridian card.

Keene points to East Terminal on the map.

KEENE
The SUV entered East Terminal six minutes after the hit. Lock the terminal and hold every camera card.

ACT TWO

INT. FBI RIVERGATE FIELD OFFICE - SECURE INTERVIEW ROOM - DAY

NADIA VALE, 30s, a confidential source with a split lip, sits across from Lena. The camera light glows red.

NADIA
Viktor Sloane didn't plan the rail yard. He only rented the SUV.

LENA
Who planned it?

NADIA
Sloane carried a Meridian card for the drop.

LENA
I'll trace the Meridian card before arraignment.

NADIA
Ask Calder. Calder can prove the route was swapped.

Lena writes CALDER? in her notebook.

NADIA
Locker 17 at East Terminal. Spare key is taped under the copy-room toner tray.

LENA
How do you know?

NADIA
Because I taped it there before I burned my wire.

Nadia leans closer, voice almost gone.

NADIA
Keene buried an OPR complaint on Malik. If he learns that from anyone but you, he walks.

Lena stops writing.

NADIA
And Project Sundial has a ghost budget line inside the Bureau. I don't know who funds it.

INT. EAST TERMINAL COPY ROOM - DAY

Rows of dead copiers. Lena wears gloves and lifts the toner tray from the oldest machine.

A brass key is taped underneath.

LENA
Locker 17.

ACT THREE

INT. EAST TERMINAL LOCKER BAY - DAY

Lena and Malik move between blue metal lockers. Malik keeps the hallway covered.

Lena uses the brass key on LOCKER 17. Inside: a black encrypted drive and a folded rail-yard access map.

LENA
Nadia was right about the toner tray. Key works, locker opens.

MALIK
Then she bought us the first honest minute of the day.

INT. FIELD OFFICE CYBER BAY - EVENING

Priya overlays tower pings on a rail map. Keene, Lena, Malik, and Darius watch.

PRIYA
Tower dump is clean. The van paused at Canal Spur for four minutes before the hit, then the SUV ghosted toward East Terminal.

Darius holds up a vial of black residue.

DARIUS
Thermite binder. Same blend used to cut courthouse lockboxes.

KEENE
Courthouse theft crew graduates to federal evidence. That is our warrant theory.

INT. FBI EVIDENCE GARAGE - NIGHT

Evidence racks stand in numbered rows. Darius photographs the black drive beside the rail-yard access map.

The sprinkler panel flashes FAULT.

A storage cabinet blooms orange from inside. Fire races along the evidence labels.

DARIUS
Everybody out!

The FBI Evidence Garage burns through the rack doors until the ceiling drops and the room is destroyed.

ACT FOUR

EXT. FEDERAL COURTHOUSE PARKING DECK - NIGHT

Lena rushes Nadia toward an unmarked sedan. Sirens echo below the concrete.

NADIA
Sloane is a courier, not the owner. Sundial owns the owner.

LENA
Who inside the Bureau signs for Sundial?

Nadia looks past Lena, terrified.

NADIA
I told you. Calder can prove --

A suppressed shot hits Nadia. Lena drags her behind the sedan.

NADIA
Don't let Keene write my 302.

Nadia dies with her hand wrapped around Lena's sleeve.

FADE OUT.
